    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0604" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/698.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I informed the President of Ecuador to-day of the probable early departure of
                    Judge Miller for Ecuador, and suggested to him the advisability executing a
                    preliminary agreement between the Ecuadorean Government and the Railway Company,
                    specifically stating the points of disagreement to be submitted to the Board of
                    Arbitration, so that its labors would be greatly expedited. He said that such an
                    agreement would not be necessary, as a memorandum agreement to the same effect
                    had been signed by the Secretary of State at Washington and the Ecuadorean
                    Minister during the past summer. No such paper is in the files of this
                        Legation.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d542-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d542-f1" n="2" xml:id="d542-f1-content">
                <p>But see Department’s August 13 to the American Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
